    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1075">

                <pb facs="1331" n="1317" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E.W./2–1145</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Peruvian
                        Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garland</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-13">February 13,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I acknowledge the receipt of your note of
                    February 11, 1945,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d1075-f1"/> in which you quote a
                    declaration of the Government of Peru stating that it recognizes a state of
                    effective belligerency between Peru on the one side and Germany and Japan on the
                    other; that it has resolved upon the adherence of Peru to the Declaration by
                    United Nations; and that you have been authorized to sign in the name of
                    Peru.</p>
                <p>The Government of the United States, as depository for the Declaration, is
                    gratified to welcome Peru formally into the ranks of the United Nations.
                    Arrangements are being made for you to sign the Declaration on February 14,
                        1945.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d1075-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1075-f1" n="20" xml:id="d1075-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1075-f2" n="21" xml:id="d1075-f2-content">
                <p>For a report of the ceremonies of signing the Declaration in behalf of Peru and
                    other states on February 14, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, February 18, 1945, pp. 234–237.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
